1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,916
On Mars, snowflakes may be cubes.

2
00:00:03,533 --> 00:00:05,702
On Earth, they have six sides.

3
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:09,705
That's how water molecules
line up when they freeze.

4
00:00:10,283 --> 00:00:13,338
But Mars also has
snow made of dry ice.

5
00:00:13,338 --> 00:00:15,412
Frozen carbon dioxide.

6
00:00:16,033 --> 00:00:18,105
Its ice has fourfold symmetry,

7
00:00:18,105 --> 00:00:20,666
so scientists expect tiny cubes.

8
00:00:21,283 --> 00:00:24,378
They fall only at the poles,
at night, under clouds.

9
00:00:24,950 --> 00:00:28,850
And as of 2022, nobody
had pictured them falling.

10
00:00:29,450 --> 00:00:31,742
On Enceladus, snow
comes from below.

11
00:00:31,742 --> 00:00:34,385
Jets spray ice, and
most falls back.

12
00:00:34,950 --> 00:00:37,033
Different world, different snow.
